<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zambia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zambia is a landlocked country in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, including part of the Central African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copperbelt">Copperbelt</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda Empire</a> place the empire's origins in a region spanning the south-east of the present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a> and parts of Zambia. It also notes that the empire's legacy remains visible in the cultural and political institutions of modern Zambia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zambia.jpg" alt="Zambia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gabriel Ellison · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Zambia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
